Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 10:08:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb: xhci-aeolia: use per-subfunction MSI-X vectors on Baikal
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary="------------false"

This is a multi-part message in MIME format.
--------------false
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8; format=fixed
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit


On Baikal, bpcie_assign_irqs() clamps nvec=1 for non-glue PCI
functions, forcing all 3 subfunctions (USB0, AHCI, USB2) of
0000:00:14.7 to share a single IRQ. The bpcie demux only maps
subfunction 0, so AHCI completions get silently dropped — causing
libata EH timeouts (5s/10s/30s) and eventual device disable.

Stock 5.4 solved this by calling pci_alloc_irq_vectors() directly
with PCI_IRQ_MSIX|PCI_IRQ_MSI, bypassing the bpcie domain entirely
for this device. Each subfunction gets its own vector.

Port the same approach: try standard PCI MSI-X/MSI allocation first
on Baikal, fall back to bpcie single-vector on failure. Use
pci_irq_vector() for lookup since MSI-X vectors may be
non-contiguous.

This fixes the internal HDD being disabled on boot due to missed
AHCI interrupts, reducing boot time from 27-130s to ~6s.
---
 drivers/usb/host/xhci-aeolia.c | 41 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 36 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)


--------------false
